IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wsa-charges`
IMPORT `wsa-qa`

-- Water Services Act 2012 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (wsa-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the answer
-- must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it is an
-- assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for the owner, with the situation FALSE and every
-- later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. These two groups are generated by the scratchpad
-- script gen_cases.py from the layer's own parameter lists.
--
-- Then, for the owner (the baseline's seat), each question is asked where its situation holds, with the answer worked
-- by hand and, beside it, the answer equal to the baseline export's on the same facts. For the occupier each question is
-- asked with the answer worked by hand from the deposited text. The facts are the baseline's (Chloe and Liam's Byford
-- house, c055, 15 July 2029, with $400 unpaid and $6 interest) where it has them; the rest is HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- The situation inputs are all BOOLEANs, so the "not read" cases cover them fully. The baseline reads its enumerations
-- (`What I am being asked to pay`, `Kind of charge`, `Term of the earlier agreement`, `What is unpaid`, `What the
-- regulations give me`) through OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31); for those, "not read" rests on the parameter script's
-- check that the role and the situation are read first.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked role` IS A Role
ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked item` IS A `What I am being asked to pay`
ASSUME `an unasked charge` IS A `Kind of charge`
ASSUME `an unasked term` IS A `Term of the earlier agreement`
ASSUME `an unasked arrear` IS A `What is unpaid`
ASSUME `an unasked purpose` IS A `Why they want to come in`
ASSUME `an unasked concession` IS A `What the regulations give me`

`as the owner` MEANS `I own land with a water, sewerage or drainage service, or a main near it`
`as the occupier` MEANS `I live in or occupy a home with a water service but do not own it, such as a tenant`

