§§ `For the owner, where the situation holds: worked by hand, and equal to the baseline`

#ASSERT `Who may charge me, as owner` `as the owner` `a fee provided for in the regulations for something done under the Act` EQUALS `the answer` "the licensee, but only in the amount the regulations provide for (s 123(1)(c))"
#ASSERT `Who may charge me, as owner` `as the owner` `something with no basis in s 123` EQUALS `the answer` "no one under s 123: a licensee's power to charge is limited to the three heads in s 123(1)"
#ASSERT `Who may charge me, as owner` `as the owner` `a charge for the water service itself` EQUALS `the answer` (`Who may charge me for this` `a charge for the water service itself`)
-- c055: statutory charges apply, the charges due are paid, the terms are kept: entitled. With charges due unpaid: not.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the service, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the service, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the service, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I entitled to the water service` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- The new lot with the main at the boundary: chargeable if the regulations say so.
#ASSERT `Can I be charged before I am connected` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I be charged before I am connected` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can I be charged before I am connected` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can I be charged for a service I am not connected to` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The developer's unpaid statutory charges follow the land; an agreed charge where no statutory charge applies does not.
#ASSERT `Can unpaid charges be recovered from me as owner` `as the owner` `a statutory water service charge` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can unpaid charges be recovered from me as owner` `as the owner` `a charge under an agreement where no statutory charge applies` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can unpaid charges be recovered from me as owner` `as the owner` `an alternative charge under an agreement in place of a statutory charge` EQUALS `yes if` (`Can the unpaid charges on my land be recovered from me as owner` `an alternative charge under an agreement in place of a statutory charge` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Who is liable, as owner` `as the owner` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `liable` `the owner only`
#ASSERT `Who is liable, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `liable` `the owner, and the tenant to the extent the regulations make a measured user liable`
#ASSERT `Who is liable, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `liable` `each owner or occupier for the share the licensee apportioned`
#ASSERT `Who is liable, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `liable` (`Who is liable for the water charges on my home` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can the charges be recovered from me if my tenant does not pay` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can the charges be recovered from me if my tenant does not pay` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can the charges still be recovered from me if my tenant does not pay` TRUE)
-- A charges term binds without notice; any other term binds only with notice: registered 21 days before possession
-- (yes), 20 days (no), or known otherwise (yes); never if the agreement says so.
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the earlier owner's agreement` `as the owner` TRUE `a term about water service charges` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the earlier owner's agreement` `as the owner` TRUE `any other term` 21 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the earlier owner's agreement` `as the owner` TRUE `any other term` 20 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the earlier owner's agreement` `as the owner` TRUE `any other term` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the earlier owner's agreement` `as the owner` TRUE `a term indemnifying the licensee` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the earlier owner's agreement` `as the owner` TRUE `any other term` 20 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I bound by the previous owner's agreement` `any other term` 20 FALSE FALSE FALSE)

#ASSERT `Can a memorial be lodged on my title` `as the owner` `statutory or alternative water service charges in arrears` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can a memorial be lodged on my title` `as the owner` `nothing, or something else` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can a memorial be lodged on my title` `as the owner` `an infrastructure contribution deferred or in arrears` EQUALS `yes if` (`Can the licensee lodge a memorial on my title` `an infrastructure contribution deferred or in arrears`)
#ASSERT `Can my dealing be registered while the memorial stands` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can my dealing be registered while the memorial stands` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can my dealing be registered while the memorial stands` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can my dealing be registered while the memorial stands` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can my dealing be registered despite a memorial` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Must the memorial be withdrawn` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must the memorial be withdrawn` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must the memorial be withdrawn` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Must the licensee withdraw the memorial` TRUE)
#ASSERT `How much do I owe when overdue` `as the owner` TRUE 400 6 0 EQUALS amount 406
#ASSERT `How much do I owe when overdue` `as the owner` TRUE 400 6 25 EQUALS amount 431
#ASSERT `How much do I owe when overdue` `as the owner` TRUE 400 6 0 EQUALS amount (`How much do I owe on an overdue bill` 400 6 0)

-- c055: 45 days overdue, living in the house, not agreeing: reduce only. 29 days: neither. Agreeing: cut off or reduce.
-- The licence forbidding it: neither.
#ASSERT `Can my supply be cut off, as owner` `as the owner` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the supply` `its flow may be reduced, but it cannot be cut off without the occupier's agreement`
#ASSERT `Can my supply be cut off, as owner` `as the owner` 29 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the supply` `neither`
#ASSERT `Can my supply be cut off, as owner` `as the owner` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the supply` `it may be cut off or its flow reduced`
#ASSERT `Can my supply be cut off, as owner` `as the owner` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the supply` `neither`
#ASSERT `Can my supply be cut off, as owner` `as the owner` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the supply` (`Can my water be cut off or reduced` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does being cut off end my debt` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does being cut off end my debt` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` `Does being cut off end what I owe`
#ASSERT `What must I pay to have my water restored` `as the owner` TRUE 406 50 FALSE EQUALS amount 456
#ASSERT `What must I pay to have my water restored` `as the owner` TRUE 406 50 TRUE EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `What must I pay to have my water restored` `as the owner` TRUE 406 50 FALSE EQUALS amount (`What must I pay before my water is restored` 406 50 FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can I claim for an interruption, as owner` `as the owner` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can I claim for an interruption, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I claim for an interruption, as owner` `as the owner` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can I claim for loss from an interruption` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is the meter presumed correct, as owner` `as the owner` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the meter presumed correct, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the meter presumed correct, as owner` `as the owner` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my meter presumed correct` FALSE)
#ASSERT `How much notice before entry, as owner` `as the owner` `to read the meter` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `notice of` 0
#ASSERT `How much notice before entry, as owner` `as the owner` `for routine inspection or maintenance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `notice of` 48
#ASSERT `How much notice before entry, as owner` `as the owner` `for routine inspection or maintenance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `notice of` (`How many hours notice must I get before entry` `for routine inspection or maintenance` TRUE TRUE)

#ASSERT `What do I get in hardship, as owner` `as the owner` EQUALS `the answer` `What does the Act give me in financial hardship`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a concession, as owner` `as the owner` `nothing` EQUALS `the answer` "not under this Act: the Act itself grants no concession; only the regulations may (ss 124(2)(o), 222(2)(c))"
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a concession, as owner` `as the owner` `an exemption` EQUALS `the answer` (`Am I entitled to a concession on my water charges` `an exemption`)
#ASSERT `Can I go to the ombudsman, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I go to the ombudsman, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can I go to the ombudsman, as owner` `as the owner` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can I go to the ombudsman, as owner` `as the owner` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can I take my dispute to the water ombudsman` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

§§ `For the occupier: worked by hand`

#ASSERT `Who may charge me, as occupier` `as the occupier` `a charge for something done or supplied as part of, or incidental to, the service` EQUALS `the answer` "the licensee providing the service, set on prudent commercial principles, subject to any limit in its licence, a code of practice or the regulations (s 123(1)(b), (2), (3))"
-- A tenant is liable only as a measured user (if the regulations say so) or for an apportioned share.
#ASSERT `Who is liable, as occupier` `as the occupier` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `liable` `the owner only`
#ASSERT `Who is liable, as occupier` `as the occupier` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `liable` `the owner, and the tenant to the extent the regulations make a measured user liable`
#ASSERT `Who is liable, as occupier` `as the occupier` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `liable` `each owner or occupier for the share the licensee apportioned`
#ASSERT `Can unpaid charges on the land be recovered from me as occupier` `as the occupier` `a statutory water service charge` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can unpaid charges on the land be recovered from me as occupier` `as the occupier` `an alternative charge under an agreement in place of a statutory charge` EQUALS no
-- Living in the home: 45 days overdue, or the owner asking, gives a reduction only unless I agree (s 95(3)).
#ASSERT `Can my supply be cut off, as occupier` `as the occupier` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the supply` `its flow may be reduced, but it cannot be cut off without the occupier's agreement`
#ASSERT `Can my supply be cut off, as occupier` `as the occupier` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the supply` `its flow may be reduced, but it cannot be cut off without the occupier's agreement`
#ASSERT `Can my supply be cut off, as occupier` `as the occupier` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the supply` `it may be cut off or its flow reduced`
#ASSERT `Can my supply be cut off, as occupier` `as the occupier` 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the supply` `neither`
#ASSERT `Can I claim for an interruption, as occupier` `as the occupier` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I claim for an interruption, as occupier` `as the occupier` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the meter presumed correct, as occupier` `as the occupier` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the meter presumed correct, as occupier` `as the occupier` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `How much notice before entry, as occupier` `as the occupier` `for routine inspection or maintenance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `notice of` 48
#ASSERT `How much notice before entry, as occupier` `as the occupier` `for routine inspection or maintenance` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `notice of` 0
#ASSERT `What do I get in hardship, as occupier` `as the occupier` EQUALS `the answer` "no hardship rule of its own: the Economic Regulation Authority's code of conduct may deal with customers in financial hardship and with suspension of services, and every licensee must comply with it as a licence condition (s 27(3)(e), (f), (4)); the code is not deposited here. Separately, the supply to an occupied dwelling cannot be cut off without the occupier's agreement (s 95(3))."
#ASSERT `Can I go to the ombudsman, as occupier` `as the occupier` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I go to the ombudsman, as occupier` `as the occupier` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
